    <item>
      <title>crosstalk</title>
      <description>comunicação cruzada entre sistemas que pareciam independentes; em biologia, interação entre vias de sinalização; em eletrônica, diafonia (interferência)

&quot;There is constant metabolic crosstalk between the gut and the liver.&quot;

[general]</description>
      <enclosure url="https://arnaldopinhoni.github.io/tv-feed/cards/crosstalk.png" type="image/png" length="0"/>
      <media:thumbnail url="https://arnaldopinhoni.github.io/tv-feed/cards/crosstalk.png"/>
      <media:content url="https://arnaldopinhoni.github.io/tv-feed/cards/crosstalk.png" medium="image"/>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:24:48 GMT</pubDate>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">vocab-crosstalk</guid>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>tender</title>
      <description>macio, tenro (carne, legumes); com pessoas, carinhoso, terno (oposto de &quot;tough&quot;)

&quot;The chicken was so tender it fell off the bone.&quot;

[general]</description>
